1
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:26,000
How about you?

2
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:27,338
Feel like fighting?

3
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:29,240
No thanks, pal.

4
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:33,858
My magic skill's gonna reach 900
soon, so I'd rather not die just yet.

5
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:35,717
At least you're honest about it.

6
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:36,976
How about you, miss?

7
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:40,537
Guess I'll pass, too.

8
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:43,000
But next time, you're going down! Oh.

9
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:46,831
Then next time, I'll make sure
to bring more friends along.

10
00:01:29,780 --> 00:01:35,100
I'm not going to see
you in the next episode.

11
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:39,396
I'm not going to say that
I'm still going to say that.

12
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:44,577
I'm still going to hear

13
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:48,837
you in the

14
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:51,980
next episode.

15
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:26,581
Hey, what's up with those flames?

16
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:27,960
There remain lights.

17
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:30,791
The players you killed can still hear you.

18
00:02:33,460 --> 00:02:35,020
Okay, now we can talk.

19
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:36,635
So, what do you want?

20
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:38,057
You want me to thank you?

21
00:02:38,140 --> 00:02:38,970
Run away?

22
00:02:39,380 --> 00:02:40,792
Or do you want to fight?

23
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:42,730
Hmm.

24
00:02:42,813 --> 00:02:45,877
If we break down what just happened, it's
one of those knight in shining armor.

25
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:47,457
saves the princess moments.

26
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:48,370
Huh?

27
00:02:48,453 --> 00:02:50,757
You could burst into tears
and throw your arms around me.

28
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:52,400
Oh, piss off, loser!

29
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:54,800
Nah, I was just kidding.

30
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:57,310
No way!

31
00:02:57,740 --> 00:03:01,360
It won't let her do that!
Watch it! Stay out of sight!

32
00:03:01,700 --> 00:03:04,377
Mommy and me are the only
ones allowed to hug Daddy!

33
00:03:04,460 --> 00:03:05,420
Wait, Daddy?

34
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:06,910
What?

35
00:03:06,993 --> 00:03:07,980
Nothing, no.

36
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:09,480
No way.

37
00:03:09,880 --> 00:03:11,998
Is that one of those private pixies?

38
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:14,760
Uh, sort of, I guess.

39
00:03:15,740 --> 00:03:16,640
Mm-hmm.

40
00:03:17,380 --> 00:03:22,262
Then how about you tell me what a Spriggan
like you is doing wandering around here.

41
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:24,520
I guess I got lost.

42
00:03:28,460 --> 00:03:30,340
How could you get that lost?

43
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:33,216
Spriggan territory's way to the east.

44
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:34,640
God, you're weird.

45
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:41,482
Anyway, thank you for saving me.

46
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:43,677
I guess I should introduce myself.

47
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:44,590
I'm Leafa.

48
00:03:44,673 --> 00:03:45,557
Nice to meet you.

49
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:48,120
I'm Kirito, and this is Yui.

50
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:57,400
Okay then, Kirito, do
you have any plans today?

51
00:03:57,760 --> 00:04:02,040
I mean, because if you don't, I
can buy you a drink as thanks.

52
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:04,537
A drink sounds awesome,
and if you don't mind,

53
00:04:04,620 --> 00:04:06,817
I'd like to pick your
brain about some stuff.

54
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:08,371
Like, what kind of stuff?

55
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:12,880
Just more about this world,
and especially about the tree.

56
00:04:13,380 --> 00:04:15,500
Oh, you mean the world tree?

57
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:17,930
Yeah, sure.

58
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:19,177
I might not look like it.

59
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:21,201
but I know a lot about this game.

60
00:04:21,940 --> 00:04:24,397
There's this neutral
village to the north of us.

61
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:26,837
It's a little out of the
way, but we can fly there.

62
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:29,060
Okay, but what about Sylvain?

63
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:30,946
Isn't that town closer to us?

64
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:34,137
You really don't know
anything about this game.

65
00:04:34,220 --> 00:04:36,500
Sylvain is Sylph territory. So?

66
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:37,857
You're not a sylph.

67
00:04:37,940 --> 00:04:42,469
If you're in their territory, you can't
attack them, but they can attack you.

68
00:04:42,980 --> 00:04:46,457
As long as I don't do anything to
provoke them, no one will attack me.

69
00:04:46,540 --> 00:04:48,422
And you'll be there, Miss Leafa.

70
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:53,717
Just call me Leafa, and if you really
want to go there, I'll take you.

71
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:56,035
I can't guarantee your safety, though.

72
00:04:56,840 --> 00:04:57,860
Let's get flying!

73
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,294
Wait, you mean you can fly
without using the controller?

74
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:07,000
Of course, can't you?

75
00:05:07,280 --> 00:05:11,117
I just learned how to use this thing, so
I'm still trying to figure everything out.

76
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:13,660
Well, there's a little trick to doing it.

77
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:16,877
Come on, turn around, but
don't access your controller.

78
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:17,790
Okay.

79
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:21,177
Can you feel where my
hand is touching you?

80
00:05:21,260 --> 00:05:22,090
Mm-hmm.

81
00:05:22,173 --> 00:05:25,897
Imagine you've got virtual bones and
muscles here spreading out into your wings.

82
00:05:25,980 --> 00:05:27,257
Then try and move them.

83
00:05:27,340 --> 00:05:29,200
Virtual bones and muscles.

84
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:32,980
Yeah, just like that.

85
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:35,600
You got it!

86
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:39,064
Okay, now try doing the
same thing, only harder.

87
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:58,540
Oh no! Daddy! Gidito! Are you okay?

88
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:08,880
How do I make it stop?

89
00:06:12,820 --> 00:06:15,580
Daddy, that's hilarious.

90
00:06:25,280 --> 00:06:27,337
Wow, this is awesome.

91
00:06:27,420 --> 00:06:28,460
I know, right?

92
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:32,602
Looks like you're starting
to get the hang of it.

93
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:35,060
Now, follow me! Okay!

94
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:38,033
Take it slow until you get better at it.

95
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:40,840
Don't worry about me.

96
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:42,100
We can go faster.

97
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:44,550
Okay.

98
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:55,680
Huh? Huh?

99
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:57,965
Is that as fast as you can go?

100
00:06:58,540 --> 00:07:00,540
Well, don't blame me if you crash.

101
00:07:12,980 --> 00:07:15,060
I can't go on, I need a break!

102
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:27,242
You're the only person I know who
can handle flying at this speed.

103
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:36,320
We made it!

104
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:41,088
Hey, we're gonna land at the
base of the central tower, okay?

105
00:07:41,820 --> 00:07:44,700
Wait, Kirito, you do
know how to land, right?

106
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:47,460
No, not really.

107
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:48,910
Uh...

108
00:07:48,993 --> 00:07:50,580
Oh, crap.

109
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:51,960
Too late now.

110
00:07:52,400 --> 00:07:53,740
You're on your own!

111
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:54,960
Wait, what?

112
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:56,480
You're kidding me!

113
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:06,240
That was so not cool.

114
00:08:06,580 --> 00:08:07,937
Stop whining already.

115
00:08:08,020 --> 00:08:09,040
I can heal you.

116
00:08:10,420 --> 00:08:13,100
Sue, Fila, Haedel, Astolu.

117
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:17,180
No way!

118
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:18,600
This is magic?

119
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:22,937
The Undine are the only ones who
specialize in high-level healing spells.

120
00:08:23,020 --> 00:08:26,377
But that's an important one anyone
can do, so you should learn it.

121
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:28,989
Different races have
different skills, huh?

122
00:08:30,140 --> 00:08:32,577
Does the Spriggan race have
anything they're good at?

123
00:08:32,660 --> 00:08:36,366
Well, you guys are good at treasure
hunting and illusion magic.

124
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:39,794
Neither of those things are
much help in battle, though.

125
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:48,000
So this is a sylph town.

126
00:08:48,980 --> 00:08:50,180
Man, it's beautiful.

127
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:51,740
I know, right?

128
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:53,870
Lipa!

129
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:56,480
Thank God you're okay!

130
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:58,260
Oh, hey, Recon.

131
00:08:59,420 --> 00:09:00,900
I knew you'd survive.

132
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:03,070
Spriggan!

133
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:05,700
No, it's okay.

134
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,059
He saved me from those salamanders.

135
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:09,740
This is my friend.

136
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:11,079
His name's Recon.

137
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:12,530
Hey there.

138
00:09:12,613 --> 00:09:13,640
My name's Kirito.

139
00:09:14,020 --> 00:09:14,960
Oh, hi.

140
00:09:15,060 --> 00:09:16,060
Nice to meet you.

141
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:19,085
Wait, what am I talking about?

142
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:20,077
I take that back.

143
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:21,237
You sure about him?

144
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:23,144
He could be a spy or something.

145
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:24,620
No, he's cool.

146
00:09:24,920 --> 00:09:28,197
I'm pretty sure if he really was a
spy, he wouldn't be such a Tetsuo.

147
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:29,620
Gee, thanks a lot.

148
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:33,257
Anyway, Sigurd and the others are
waiting for you at the tavern.

149
00:09:33,340 --> 00:09:34,340
Oh, that's right.

150
00:09:37,260 --> 00:09:40,020
On second thought, I can't go today. Huh?

151
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:42,200
You're not going? Nope.

152
00:09:42,660 --> 00:09:46,137
I sort of promised Kirito I'd
buy him a drink for saving me.

153
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:47,050
See you later!

154
00:09:47,133 --> 00:09:49,120
Wait, you don't have to...

155
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:51,480
Oh, Lipia!

156
00:10:04,460 --> 00:10:06,377
Is that retcon guy your boyfriend?

157
00:10:06,460 --> 00:10:08,401
Yeah, are the two of you in love?

158
00:10:08,560 --> 00:10:09,390
No!

159
00:10:09,473 --> 00:10:10,303
We're not in love!

160
00:10:10,386 --> 00:10:12,373
but we're just in the same party is all.

161
00:10:12,580 --> 00:10:15,317
I don't know, from where I was
standing, you guys seemed tight.

162
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:17,357
Whatever, I know him in real life.

163
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:20,417
We go to the same school and
we're classmates, but that's it.

164
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:21,330
Mm-hmm.

165
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:25,620
Anyway, bottoms up.

166
00:10:25,980 --> 00:10:27,804
And thanks again for saving me.

167
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:34,977
Those guys in the forest
were playing pretty rough.

168
00:10:35,060 --> 00:10:37,737
Are Gangs of PKers normal
for this game or what?

169
00:10:37,820 --> 00:10:41,097
Well, for one thing, the salamander
and sylph races never got along.

170
00:10:41,180 --> 00:10:45,297
But those guys were organized, and
that wasn't happening until recently.

171
00:10:45,380 --> 00:10:46,210
I don't know.

172
00:10:46,293 --> 00:10:49,817
If you ask me, they're gearing up
to try to clear the world tree soon.

173
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:53,277
Actually, I was hoping you could tell
me what you knew about the world tree.

174
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:55,317
Oh, yeah, you mentioned it before.

175
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:56,737
Why do you want to know?

176
00:10:56,820 --> 00:10:59,291
I want to get to the top as soon as I can.

177
00:11:00,380 --> 00:11:01,240
Join the club.

178
00:11:01,460 --> 00:11:03,377
Every player wants to get to the top.

179
00:11:03,460 --> 00:11:06,695
You could say that's the
grand quest of Alfheim Online.

180
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:07,920
What do you mean?

181
00:11:08,280 --> 00:11:10,957
You know how you're limited
in how high you can fly?

182
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:11,960
The fact is,

183
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:15,837
